      "id": "followups/molly-behavior-unit-tests",
      "source_commit": "284a8b47c8a7f613551f6b8b2cadb565b70c081b",
      "description": "Fix unit tests that did not match Molly behavior in the Signal 8.33.2 port\n\nApply remote config overrides in internal builds. Molly derives internalUser\nfrom the build type, not from the service, so loading overrides must ask\ninternalUser instead of the service's android.internalUser value, which Molly\ndoes not read. Overrides were never applied before.\n\nAdapt the Signal 8.33.2 tests to intended Molly differences:\n\n- IndividualSettingsViewModelTest stubs getLinkedDeviceCount, which Molly\n  adds to the contact details. Molly has no profile badges and no donations,\n  so badge and donate clicks produce no action.\n- RemoteConfigOverrideTest runs as an internal debug build instead of faking\n  the service's internalUser flag.\n- NotificationProfileDetailsScreenTest builds the expected schedule text with\n  formatHours, since Molly formats times with the locale's best pattern.\n- StoryContextMenuTest sets up app dependencies itself rather than relying on\n  another test having initialized PartAuthority.\n- The app-settings, registration, media-viewer and media-send tests expect\n  Molly's music-labelled waves icon, Molly name in the notification warning,\n  version row click event, always-shown link device button, a Material 3 theme\n  for the Molly video player layout, and Molly's minimum SDK (27).",
      "ai_generated": true,
      "before_tree": "2a78679e2344ddf3fc6bbaa5079d5f8a274d3dda",
