    {
      "id": "followups/unifiedpush-registration-retry",
      "description": "Recover from a failed UnifiedPush registration visibly and boundedly\n\nAI-assisted compatibility changes. A failed distributor registration only\nshowed a notification and never retried, so UnifiedPush could stay broken\nsilently. Now the failure shows in UnifiedPush settings with a Retry\nregistration action, and one automatic UnifiedPushRefreshJob runs per failure\nepisode (network constraint, three attempts, six-hour lifespan) instead of an\nendless background retry. Choosing a distributor, or a successful endpoint\ncallback, clears the failure. Nothing touches the encrypted store while the\napp is locked.\n\nAI-Generated: true\n\nBased-On-Source-Commit: 15f7295a60711b116e83fda111b120018412f7be",
      "source_commit": "b3c3bac2229b2e7a4a251fd4377a6e7d56868677",
